WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:20.385
In every small city, there are young men with too much money and too little to do.

2
00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:23.886
Monsieur Bamatabois was one of these idle young men.

3
00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:30.688
One evening that winter he stood outside a cafe, smoking and watching a poor young woman walk up

4
00:00:30.728 --> 00:00:31.488
and down the street.

5
00:00:32.436 --> 00:00:35.919
He was wrapped warmly in a cloak while she wore only a dress.

6
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.982
Every time she passed, he called out insults.

7
00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:41.384
"How ugly you are!

8
00:00:41.904 --> 00:00:43.405
Do you know you've lost your teeth?"

9
00:00:44.346 --> 00:00:46.948
The woman ignored him and continued to pace the sidewalk.

10
00:00:47.509 --> 00:00:49.871
Her failure to respond annoyed Bamatabois.

11
00:00:50.652 --> 00:00:54.875
So the next time she passed, he grabbed a handful of snow and tossed it down the back

12
00:00:54.895 --> 00:00:55.476
of her dress.

13
00:00:55.496 --> 00:01:00.200
"Why, you The woman swore at Bamatabois and rushed to attack him.

14
00:01:01.096 --> 00:01:02.356
A crowd began to gather.

15
00:01:02.957 --> 00:01:06.978
Bamatabois defended himself as the woman scratched his face and kicked his shins.

16
00:01:07.778 --> 00:01:09.758
The woman was Fantine.

17
00:01:11.419 --> 00:01:16.320
Suddenly a tall man advanced from the crowd, seized her by the waist, and said, "You're under arrest

18
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.060
for assault."

19
00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:20.341
Fantine looked up and stopped screaming at once.

20
00:01:21.002 --> 00:01:24.362
She shuddered with terror because she knew that he was a policeman.

21
00:01:25.243 --> 00:01:26.083
It was Javert.

22
00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:29.484
Meanwhile Bamatabois used that moment to slip away.

23
00:01:30.292 --> 00:01:35.454
Javert quickly broke up the crowd and walked toward the police station, dragging Fantine behind him.

24
00:01:36.454 --> 00:01:39.115
At the station Javert wrote out the charges against her.

25
00:01:39.855 --> 00:01:43.316
When he finished writing, he said to the guard, "Take this woman to jail.

26
00:01:44.056 --> 00:01:45.516
She has attacked an honest citizen."

27
00:01:46.137 --> 00:01:51.158
Then, turning to Fantine, he said, "You're sentenced to six months."

28
00:01:51.218 --> 00:01:52.599
"No!" screamed Fantine.

29
00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:54.619
"What will happen to my child?

30
00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:57.220
Cosette will be thrown into the street.

31
00:01:58.364 --> 00:02:00.886
I was wrong to attack the gentleman and ruin his hat.

32
00:02:01.366 --> 00:02:01.887
Where is he?

33
00:02:01.907 --> 00:02:03.708
I want to beg his pardon.

34
00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:05.429
Oh, please have pity on me!"

35
00:02:05.449 --> 00:02:09.252
"It's too late for that," said Javert.

36
00:02:09.272 --> 00:02:10.533
"Take her away!"

37
00:02:10.553 --> 00:02:12.054
"Just a moment!"

38
00:02:12.415 --> 00:02:15.377
A man had entered the room while Fantine was pleading with Javert.

39
00:02:16.278 --> 00:02:17.338
Javert turned around.

40
00:02:17.358 --> 00:02:18.739
"Yes, Mayor Madeleine?"

41
00:02:18.759 --> 00:02:21.281
"So you are the mayor!"

42
00:02:21.602 --> 00:02:24.484
hissed Fantine, and she spat in his face.

43
00:02:25.288 --> 00:02:28.750
The mayor wiped his face and said to Javert, "Set this woman free."

44
00:02:29.671 --> 00:02:32.912
Javert could not believe what he was hearing, and neither could Fantine.

45
00:02:32.932 --> 00:02:36.935
"This is the same mayor who had me fired from his factory!"

46
00:02:37.255 --> 00:02:38.055
cried Fantine.

47
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:42.178
"And all because he listened to the gossip of old women."

48
00:02:42.198 --> 00:02:44.879
"I can't let her go," said Javert.

49
00:02:44.899 --> 00:02:47.501
"She has insulted you and attacked a citizen."

50
00:02:47.521 --> 00:02:51.283
"I was passing down the street when you arrested her," said the mayor.

51
00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:53.364
"I talked to some people in the crowd.

52
00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:56.076
She didn't do anything wrong.

53
00:02:56.677 --> 00:02:58.717
It was Bamatabois who attacked her."

54
00:02:59.497 --> 00:03:00.818
Javert was not moved.

55
00:03:00.838 --> 00:03:04.499
"I have the authority here, and I say she goes to jail."

56
00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:09.560
"Perhaps you should check the law regarding illegal imprisonment," said Madeleine.

57
00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.701
Javert glared at him, but the mayor stared right back.

58
00:03:13.721 --> 00:03:14.702
"Get out!"

59
00:03:15.222 --> 00:03:16.462
said the mayor to Javert.

60
00:03:17.522 --> 00:03:19.883
Javert looked startled, but recovered quickly.

61
00:03:20.503 --> 00:03:23.104
He bowed to the mayor and left the police station.

62
00:03:23.932 --> 00:03:28.214
Later that night Javert sat down and wrote a letter to the chief of police in Paris.

63
00:03:29.155 --> 00:03:33.077
Meanwhile Fantine had stood by the door and watched Javert leave.

64
00:03:33.798 --> 00:03:35.218
She did not know what to think.

65
00:03:36.079 --> 00:03:41.282
The man who had saved her was none other than Mayor Madeleine, the person she blamed for all

66
00:03:41.362 --> 00:03:41.982
her woes.

67
00:03:42.842 --> 00:03:46.384
At the very moment when she had insulted him, he had rescued her.

68
00:03:48.005 --> 00:03:52.628
She quickly felt her hatred melting away, replaced by feelings of warmth toward him.

69
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.723
Madeleine turned to her and said, "I had no idea that you had left my factory.

70
00:03:58.283 --> 00:03:59.644
Why didn't you come to me for help?"

71
00:03:59.664 --> 00:04:04.666
"Because the supervisor told me that you were the one who wanted me fired."

72
00:04:04.686 --> 00:04:06.487
"Oh, you poor woman!"

73
00:04:06.808 --> 00:04:08.529
Madeleine's eyes filled with tears.

74
00:04:08.549 --> 00:04:11.951
"I'll have your child brought here, or pay for you to go to her.

75
00:04:12.731 --> 00:04:15.212
You shall live here, or in Paris, or wherever you like.

76
00:04:15.693 --> 00:04:17.854
You shall do no more work unless you want to.

77
00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:21.336
I'll give you all the money you need, and I'll pay all your debts.

78
00:04:22.144 --> 00:04:25.267
I'll be responsible for you and your child from now on."

79
00:04:26.128 --> 00:04:28.290
This was more than Fantine could bear.

80
00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.331
To have Cosette by her side!

81
00:04:30.832 --> 00:04:32.633
To live free from debt and worry!

82
00:04:33.374 --> 00:04:36.837
She was unable to say anything to Mayor Madeleine and could only sob.

83
00:04:37.618 --> 00:04:41.201
Her legs gave way, and she sank to her knees before the mayor.

84
00:04:41.841 --> 00:04:44.944
She reached out to kiss his hand, and then she fainted.

85
00:04:46.365 --> 00:04:49.408
The mayor had Fantine taken to the infirmary in his house.

86
00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:55.163
A violent fever came over her, and she spent part of the night in delirious ravings.

87
00:04:55.963 --> 00:04:57.344
Finally she fell asleep.

88
00:04:57.844 --> 00:05:01.846
When she awoke the next morning, the mayor was praying by her bedside.

89
00:05:02.607 --> 00:05:04.588
That day he wrote to the Thenardiers.

90
00:05:05.268 --> 00:05:10.051
Fantine owed them more than one hundred francs; Madeleine sent three hundred.

91
00:05:10.731 --> 00:05:15.554
He told them to bring Cosette to Fantine, who was sick and desperately wanted her child.

92
00:05:16.074 --> 00:05:18.135
His letter astonished Monsieur Thenardier.

93
00:05:18.155 --> 00:05:19.736
"Look at this!"

94
00:05:20.096 --> 00:05:21.497
Thenardier said to his wife.

95
00:05:21.517 --> 00:05:25.800
"Some silly fellow must have fallen in love with Fantine."

96
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.102
Monsieur Thenardier replied to the mayor with a request for more money.

97
00:05:30.603 --> 00:05:33.064
He included bills from the doctor and the pharmacy.

98
00:05:33.685 --> 00:05:36.927
The bills were real, but they were for Eponine and Azelma.

99
00:05:37.627 --> 00:05:40.509
Thenardier merely substituted Cosette's name for theirs.

100
00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:45.532
The mayor immediately sent the money and wrote, "Bring Cosette quickly."

101
00:05:46.272 --> 00:05:50.715
"We aren't letting go of this girl," said Thenardier to his wife when he read that note.

102
00:05:50.735 --> 00:05:52.896
"She's a gold mine."

103
00:05:53.796 --> 00:05:57.438
Meanwhile Fantine had not recovered and was still in the infirmary.

104
00:05:58.339 --> 00:06:03.942
The mayor visited her twice a day, and each time she asked, "Shall I see Cosette soon?"

105
00:06:04.643 --> 00:06:06.704
He replied, "Perhaps tomorrow.

106
00:06:07.384 --> 00:06:08.845
I expect her at any moment."

107
00:06:09.505 --> 00:06:11.567
And Fantine's pale face brightened.

108
00:06:11.587 --> 00:06:13.848
"Oh, how happy I'll be!"

109
00:06:14.644 --> 00:06:17.345
But her condition was growing worse from week to week.

110
00:06:18.085 --> 00:06:20.025
One day the doctor listened to her lungs.

111
00:06:20.886 --> 00:06:25.447
He shook his head and then took the mayor aside for a private conversation.

112
00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:28.928
"Doesn't Fantine have a daughter that she's eager to see?"

113
00:06:29.308 --> 00:06:30.088
asked the doctor.

114
00:06:30.108 --> 00:06:32.349
"Yes," replied the mayor.

115
00:06:32.369 --> 00:06:37.870
"Then you'd better get the child here soon because Fantine is going to die."

116
00:06:39.591 --> 00:06:42.471
Madeleine shuddered and went back into Fantine's room.

117
00:06:42.491 --> 00:06:44.392
"What did the doctor say?"

118
00:06:44.828 --> 00:06:45.608
asked Fantine.

119
00:06:46.549 --> 00:06:47.729
The mayor tried to smile.

120
00:06:47.749 --> 00:06:52.091
"He told us to bring Cosette at once because that will make you well."

121
00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.772
"Oh, he's right!"

122
00:06:54.152 --> 00:06:54.692
she cried.

123
00:06:54.712 --> 00:06:57.073
"But what's the matter with the Thenardiers?

124
00:06:57.553 --> 00:06:59.234
Why are they keeping her from me?"

125
00:07:00.014 --> 00:07:03.036
The mayor did not tell her that they were full of excuses.

126
00:07:03.696 --> 00:07:07.897
They said that Cosette was too fragile to travel in the winter, and that they were still adding

127
00:07:07.937 --> 00:07:09.978
up the amount of money they had spent on her.

128
00:07:09.998 --> 00:07:13.760
"I will send someone for Cosette," said the mayor to Fantine.

129
00:07:14.396 --> 00:07:16.297
"If necessary, I will go myself."

130
00:07:17.238 --> 00:07:23.561
He wrote out a letter for Fantine, which she signed: Dear Monsieur Thenardier: You will deliver Cosette to

131
00:07:23.601 --> 00:07:24.722
the bearer of this letter.

132
00:07:25.462 --> 00:07:27.403
He will pay all the money that I owe you.

133
00:07:27.944 --> 00:07:29.585
Sincerely, Fantine
